  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: As the ridging and HPC pattern over the\nsouthwestern CONUS breaks down this week an upper level shortwave\nwill ride zonal flow over the western CONUS through the Great\nBasin tonight. Boundary forcing and perhaps some diurnal\ninstability will be enough to initiate some low probability\nisolated storm activity over northern NV this evening and tonight,\nbut the moisture profile over the area doesn't offer much in the\nway of support. PW values hovering around half an inch combined\nwith elevated bases will lead to dry convection if storms do\ninitiate. Little to no accumulating rainfall is expected with this\nsystem.\n\nThe area will be under a short-lived post frontal regime on\nTuesday before ridging builds back into the southwestern CONUS for\nmuch of the rest of this week. This will allow warm afternoon high\ntemperatures to continue through Thursday ranging 10 to 15 degrees\nabove normal in the low to mid 80s. \n\nBeyond Friday the ridging over the region gets squeezed eastward \nas a large longwave ULT pushes into the Pacific Northwest Friday \nevening. This will tighten the gradient over the area bringing the\npotential for gusty winds and impactful precipitation by the \nweekend.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Very low confidence exists in\nevening shower and thunderstorm activity Monday evening. That\nbeing said NBM represented even low chances very poorly so a\ncombination of SST and SerpISC was used to increase Pops enough to\ngenerate some low chance IsoT across northern NV from 22Z to 04Z\ntonight. Moderate confidence exists in continued warm temperatures\neach afternoon through this week. Very low confidence exists in\nthe potential for an impactful storm system through the area this\nweekend.",
